{"parentUuid":"efedfc3c-8b64-429e-81e0-1eeb55f5c689","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01KqqvYQjYb9faAbRKLfrcLf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Search works against the real brain (returns doc + history hits) — and the TUI's `s` key calls that exact path. The Search-tab column count (2 cells / 2 columns) is consistent and `TestTabCycleNoPanic` now cycles all 6 tabs including Search, so the crash class that bit us before is covered.\n\nGiven a real crash slipped through last time, let me run one more focused audit on the new surface (search state machine + `add` + regression of the prior fixes) before I call it verified."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1240,"cache_read_input_tokens":390628,"output_tokens":5037,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5037,"cache_read_input_tokens":390628,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1240},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cc88uC1nJt9LCufSryT17","type":"assistant","uuid":"afd16fa6-2fb6-4ffb-becd-54e6df07bfa0","timestamp":"2026-06-17T03:40:19.933Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"afd16fa6-2fb6-4ffb-becd-54e6df07bfa0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01KqqvYQjYb9faAbRKLfrcLf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LtArp49cxnvLxacHd4trqh","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'audit-brain-dash-v2',\n  description: 'Adversarial audit of the new search-in-TUI + `entire brain add` + prior-fix regressions',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Review', detail: 'parallel reviewers per dimension' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'refute each finding by reading the code' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst REPO = '/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain'\n\nconst FINDINGS_SCHEMA = {\n  type: 'object', additionalProperties: false,\n  properties: {\n    findings: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object', additionalProperties: false,\n        properties: {\n          title: { type: 'string' },\n          file: { type: 'string' },\n          line: { type: 'string' },\n          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['crash', 'bug', 'security', 'correctness', 'minor', 'nit'] },\n          detail: { type: 'string' },\n          suggested_fix: { type: 'string' },\n        },\n        required: ['title', 'file', 'severity', 'detail', 'suggested_fix'],\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  required: ['findings'],\n}\nconst VERDICT_SCHEMA = {\n  type: 'object', additionalProperties: false,\n  properties: {\n    real: { type: 'boolean' },\n    reasoning: { type: 'string' },\n    confidence: { type: 'string', enum: ['high', 'medium', 'low'] },\n  },\n  required: ['real', 'reasoning', 'confidence'],\n}\n\nconst base = `You are auditing newly-added Go code in ${REPO} for the \\`entire brain dash\\` TUI. Two features were just added and four earlier bugs were fixed:\nNEW: (a) in-dashboard SEARCH — an \\`s\\` key opens a search prompt; on submit an async tea.Cmd runs a SearchFunc, results land on a new TabSearch. Code: internal/tui/tui.go (SearchFunc, searchResultMsg, updateSearching, runSearchCmd, the s-key + searching-mode routing, resize search width, mouse gating), internal/tui/viewmodels.go (TabSearch, SearchResult, count/filterKey/openTarget/ParseTab cases), internal/tui/table.go (TabSearch columns+rows), internal/tui/detail.go (renderSearchResult, renderSearchEmpty), internal/cli/dash.go (brainSearchFunc adapting retrieveUnified + dashSearchLimit, tui.Run call). (b) \\`entire brain add <repo-url>\\` — internal/cli/add.go (runBrainAdd, buildClonedBrain via os.Executable()+ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT, repoDirName, isGitCheckout), registered in internal/cli/root.go CREATE group.\nPRIOR FIXES to confirm still hold: switchTab does m.table.SetRows(nil) before SetColumns (tui.go); renderHome source lines use lipgloss MaxWidth not truncate (detail.go); brainRelPath rejects ../ traversal (dash.go); osc8 link wired into writeOpenHint (detail.go).\nInvariants: the TUI is read-only/no-egress; search uses retrieveUnified (internal/cli/retrieve.go) which reads local index files only.\nCross-check structs: unifiedResult (retrieve.go:16), retrieveUnified (retrieve.go:48), exportSession (export.go), CommandRunner (runner.go:12), runRefresh (refresh.go:95).\nREAD the actual files before judging. Report ONLY real, evidence-grounded issues at a specific file:line, each with a concrete suggested_fix. An empty findings list is a valid, good answer.`\n\nconst DIMENSIONS = [\n  { key: 'search-fsm', prompt: `${base}\\n\\nDIMENSION: the search state machine & TabSearch safety. Scrutinize: key routing precedence (can filtering+searching both be active? does the searching branch correctly precede the main key switch? does esc/enter behave?); updateSearching empty-query handling; the async runSearchCmd closure capturing m.searchFn (is it safe to run in a goroutine — does it touch shared mutable Model state?); searchResultMsg handling (does it reset cursor/columns safely like switchTab? could it panic via the same SetColumns-vs-stale-rows path?); TabSearch column count (2) vs rowsFor cell count (2) — must match or bubbles/table panics; the empty Search tab detail path (idx<0); resize of m.search width; mouse gating during search; whether opening search from a non-Home tab then submitting leaves stale state. Also confirm TestTabCycleNoPanic actually covers TabSearch.` },\n  { key: 'add-cmd', prompt: `${base}\\n\\nDIMENSION: the \\`add\\` command. Scrutinize internal/cli/add.go: buildClonedBrain re-execs os.Executable() with args [\"refresh\"] and ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT — is os.Executable() correct when the binary is dispatched as the \\`entire brain\\` plugin (vs standalone)? Does \\`entire-brain refresh\\` actually build for the cloned dir given cwd+env? The refresh stages shell the host \\`entire\\` CLI (entireBinary/semBinary default \"entire\") — is the PATH dependency handled/communicated on failure? repoURL is passed to git via opts.Runner.Run (exec, no shell) — confirm no command-injection; repoDirName edge cases (URLs with query strings, trailing slashes, nested groups like gitlab a/b/c, empty); dest path safety; clone-skip via isGitCheckout; best-effort fetch vs hard error semantics; whether build failure correctly degrades to guidance rather than a hard error. Is registering add in CREATE group correct?` },\n  { key: 'regress-integration', prompt: `${base}\\n\\nDIMENSION: regression of the 4 prior fixes + dash.go search wiring + no-egress. Re-verify each prior fix is intact and correct (switchTab SetRows(nil) ordering; renderHome MaxWidth; brainRelPath ../ containment via filepath.Rel; osc8 in writeOpenHint). Then audit brainSearchFunc in dash.go: field mapping unifiedResult->SearchResult, OpenPath via brainRelPath (containment applied to search-result paths too?), OpenLine, dashSearchLimit, modeLexical choice, error propagation to searchResultMsg. Confirm the whole dash + search path is read-only/no-egress (no writes, no network, no agent runner) — note retrieveUnified only reads local files. Flag any inconsistency or missed containment.` },\n]\n\nlog(`v2 audit: ${DIMENSIONS.length} dimensions over search + add + prior-fix regressions`)\n\nconst results = await pipeline(\n  DIMENSIONS,\n  (d) => agent(d.prompt, { label: `review:${d.key}`, phase: 'Review', schema: FINDINGS_SCHEMA }),\n  (review, d) => {\n    const findings = (review && review.findings) || []\n    return parallel(findings.map((f) => () =>\n      agent(\n        `${base}\\n\\nA reviewer (dimension \"${d.key}\") raised this finding. REFUTE it by reading the actual code. Default real=false unless, after reading the cited file:line and surrounding code, you confirm it is a genuine issue a maintainer would fix. Reject speculative, stylistic-without-impact, or already-handled items.\\n\\nFINDING\\ntitle: ${f.title}\\nfile: ${f.file}\\nline: ${f.line || '?'}\\nseverity: ${f.severity}\\ndetail: ${f.detail}\\nsuggested_fix: ${f.suggested_fix}\\n\\nReturn real=true only for a real defect; explain from the code.`,\n        { label: `verify:${d.key}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICT_SCHEMA }\n      ).then((v) => ({ ...f, dimension: d.key, verdict: v }))\n    ))\n  }\n)\n\nconst all = results.flat().filter(Boolean)\nconst confirmed = all.filter((f) => f.verdict && f.verdict.real)\nlog(`raised ${all.length}, confirmed ${confirmed.length}`)\nreturn { confirmed, raisedCount: all.length, confirmedCount: confirmed.length }\n","description":"Audit search + add + prior-fix regressions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1240,"cache_read_input_tokens":390628,"output_tokens":5037,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5037,"cache_read_input_tokens":390628,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1240,"cache_cr