{"parentUuid":"ab31bad9-d74f-487c-ae6f-fe8ede4838fa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wgrbwnsmc</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01LtArp49cxnvLxacHd4trqh</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-Documents-Coding-entire-brain/4e09703c-666f-441f-9b82-52efaa7da599/tasks/wgrbwnsmc.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Adversarial audit of the new search-in-TUI + `entire brain add` + prior-fix regressions\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"confirmed\":[{\"title\":\"A committed filter from the prior tab silently hides in-dashboard search results\",\"file\":\"internal/tui/tui.go\",\"line\":\"125-142\",\"severity\":\"bug\",\"detail\":\"The searchResultMsg handler switches to TabSearch and calls rebuildVisible() but never clears m.filter, unlike switchTab() (line 213) which does m.filter.SetValue(\\\"\\\"). A filter is committed (not just typed) by pressing Enter in updateFiltering (lines 264-267), which sets m.filtering=false while deliberately keeping m.filter.Value() so the filter stays applied. Because the main key switch only gates / and s behind !m.filtering (lines 147-152), the user can legitimately reach search with a non-empty committed filter. Sequence: on Facts, press '/', type a string, Enter (filter committed); then press 's', type a query, Enter. When searchResultMsg lands, rebuildVisible() (line 141 -&gt; line 398) applies q = m.filter.Value() over the TabSearch results via filterKey(TabSearch, i), silently dropping any search hit that doesn't also contain the stale filter text. The tab bar still shows Search (N) from m.snap.count(TabSearch) (the unfiltered total, tui.go:473 / viewmodels.go:210-211), so the count and the visible list disagree and real results vanish. I confirmed this with a focused test: 2 search results existed, a stale committed filter 'zzznomatch' made visible=0 while the tab bar reported Search (2).\",\"suggested_fix\":\"In the searchResultMsg case (around line 136-141), clear the carried-over filter before rebuilding, mirroring switchTab: add m.filter.SetValue(\\\"\\\") (and, for consistency, m.filtering = false is already implied) immediately before m.rebuildVisible() so search results are shown unfiltered and the Search (N) count matches the visible rows.\",\"dimension\":\"search-fsm\",\"verdict\":{\"real\":true,\"reasoning\":\"Confirmed by reading the code. The finding's full causal chain holds:\\n\\n1. A filter is committed (not cleared) via the Enter path. internal/tui/tui.go:264-267 updateFiltering \\\"enter\\\" sets m.filtering=false and m.filter.Blur() but intentionally does NOT clear the value; only the \\\"esc\\\" path (lines 258-262) calls m.filter.SetValue(\\\"\\\"). So m.filter.Value() can be non-empty while m.filtering==false.\\n\\n2. With m.filtering==false, the s-key is reachable. The main key switch returns early only for m.filtering (147-149) and m.searching (150-152); the Search binding is matched at tui.go:164-170, which sets m.searching/Focus and clears only m.search (not m.filter). runSearchCmd (297-306) merely calls fn. So the committed filter survives to the result handler untouched.\\n\\n3. The searchResultMsg handler (tui.go:125-142) switches m.tab=TabSearch, resets columns/cursor, and calls m.rebuildVisible() (line 141) but never clears m.filter — unlike switchTab (tui.go:213) which does m.filter.SetValue(\\\"\\\").\\n\\n4. rebuildVisible (tui.go:397-410) reads q = strings.ToLower(strings.TrimSpace(m.filter.Value())) and keeps only indices where strings.Contains(m.snap.filterKey(m.tab, i), q). filterKey has a real TabSearch case (viewmodels.go:237-239), so a stale filter silently drops every search hit whose Source/Text/Path/Heading doesn't also contain the filter text.\\n\\n5. The tab bar count disagrees: renderTabs (tui.go:466-481) prints \\\"Search (%d)\\\" using m.snap.count(t), and count(TabSearch) returns len(s.Search) (viewmodels.go:210-211) — the UNfiltered total. So the header shows e.g. Search (2) while the visible list is empty, and real results vanish with no indication of why.\\n\\nThis is a reachable, non-contrived user flow (commit a filter on Facts with '/'+Enter, then press 's', search) that silently hides correct results and produces a count/visible mismatch. The suggested fix is correct and minimal: add m.filter.SetValue(\\\"\\\") immediately before m.rebuildVisible() in the searchResultMsg case (around tui.go:136-141), mirroring switchTab. A maintainer would fix this.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}},{\"title\":\"repoDirName can return \\\"..\\\" or \\\".\\\", making dest the parent/current dir and fetching into an unintended repo\",\"file\":\"internal/cli/add.go\",\"line\":\"106-133, 50, 63\",\"severity\":\"bug\",\"detail\":\"repoDirName splits the URL path on '/' and joins the last two non-empty segments with '_', but it does not reject '.' or '..' segments. For a crafted URL whose path tail is a single dot-dot segment (e.g. `entire brain add https://h/..` or scp-form `git@h:..`), repoDirName returns \\\"..\\\"; `https://h/.` returns \\\".\\\". Then dest = filepath.Join(flags.dir, name): with the default --dir=\\\".\\\" this yields dest=\\\"..\\\" (the parent directory) or \\\".\\\" (the current directory). isGitCheckout(dest) is then evaluated against that real directory: if the parent/cwd is itself a git checkout, add prints \\\"already present, skipping\\\" and proceeds to run `git fetch --quiet origin refs/heads/entire/*:refs/heads/entire/*` *inside the user's own surrounding repository* (add.go:63), creating refs/heads/entire/* branches there from whatever that repo's origin exposes — a mutation of an unintended repo. If it is not a checkout, `git clone &lt;url&gt; ..` fails on a non-empty dest, which is merely a confusing error. Verified empirically: repoDirName(\\\"https://h/..\\\")==\\\"..\\\", repoDirName(\\\"https://h/.\\\")==\\\".\\\". Multi-segment '..' (e.g. https://h/a/..) is neutralized because the '/' is replaced by '_' (yields \\\"a_..\\\"), so only a trailing single-dot/dot-dot path segment triggers it. Low probability (requires a malformed URL) but a real input-validation gap that can write into a repo the user did not name.\",\"suggested_fix\":\"After deriving name, reject reserved/traversal names before computing dest: e.g. `if name == \\\".\\\" || name == \\\"..\\\" || strings.ContainsAny(name, \\\"/\\\\\\\\\\\") { return fmt.Errorf(\\\"invalid_repo_url: cannot derive a safe directory name from %q\\\", repoURL) }`. Equivalently, validate that filepath.Clean(dest) stays within flags.dir (dest != flags.dir and dest is not an ancestor of flags.dir) before the isGitCheckout/clone/fetch steps.\",\"dimension\":\"add-cmd\",\"verdict\":{\"real\":true,\"reasoning\":\"Confirmed by reading the code and empirically running repoDirName. The finding is accurate.\\n\\nTrace (internal/cli/add.go):\\n- Line 30-33: cobra Args is only ExactArgs(1); no URL validation. args[0] is passed straight to runBrainAdd.\\n- Line 46-49: the only guard is `name == \\\"\\\"`. repoDirName never returns \\\".\\\" or \\\"..\\\" as empty, so they pass.\\n- repoDirName (106-133): splits the post-host path on '/', drops empty segments, and for a single segment returns it verbatim with no reserved-name check. Verified empirically (compiled+ran the exact function):\\n  repoDirName(\\\"https://h/..\\\") == \\\"..\\\"  and  repoDirName(\\\"https://h/.\\\") == \\\".\\\"  (also git@h:.. and git@h:.). Multi-segment \\\"https://h/a/..\\\" correctly neutralizes to \\\"a_..\\\" because '/' becomes '_', so only a trailing single dot/dot-dot segment triggers it — exactly as the finding states.\\n- Line 50: dest = filepath.Join(flags.dir, name). With default --dir=\\\".\\\", filepath.Join(\\\".\\\",\\\"..\\\")==\\\"..\\\", filepath.Join(\\\".\\\",\\\".\\\")==\\\".\\\".\\n- Line 53: isGitCheckout(dest) checks os.Stat(dest/.git). If the user is inside a git repo (the common case), \\\"..\\\" and/or \\\".\\\" resolve to that real checkout, so this returns true and the clone is skipped (\\\"already present, skipping\\\").\\n- Line 63: git fetch is then run with dir=dest (runner.go:18-22 sets cmd.Dir=dir), i.e. inside the user's own surrounding repo. The refspec refs/heads/entire/*:refs/heads/entire/* writes into local refs/heads/entire/* of that repo, pulling from that repo's own `origin` (repoURL is not passed to fetch). This is a real state mutation of a repository the user never named, in a tool otherwise intended to be non-destructive toward the user's environment.\\n\\nIf the parent/cwd is not a git checkout, the clone instead runs `git clone &lt;url&gt; ..`/`.` into a non-empty dir and fails with a confusing error — the lesser case the finding also acknowledges.\\n\\nThis is a genuine input-validation gap wit\n... (truncated 9184 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-Documents-Coding-entire-brain/4e09703c-666f-441f-9b82-52efaa7da599/tasks/wgrbwnsmc.output)</result>\n<usage><agent_count>9</agent_count><subagent_tokens>427057</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>105</tool_uses><duration_ms>253055</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"566f0d76-1a51-4201-8f20-d315f6680299","timestamp":"2026-06-17T03:45:10.502Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
